MediaPipe

The xcframeworks published with each release of this repository are built from
the MediaPipeTasksVision and MediaPipeTasksCommon binaries published by
Google. The upstream version is recorded in MEDIAPIPE_VERSION and in each
release's notes, and MEDIAPIPE_SOURCES lists the exact archives used.

  Copyright The MediaPipe Authors.
  https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe

MediaPipe is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The complete
license text is provided as LICENSE-MediaPipe.

Stripe changed the upstream binaries as follows. No MediaPipe source code was
changed, and the changes are made by Scripts/refresh_artifacts.sh.

MediaPipeTasksVision.xcframework and MediaPipeTasksCommon.xcframework:

  * Removed the x86_64 architecture from the simulator slice, and renamed that
    slice from ios-arm64_x86_64-simulator to ios-arm64-simulator.
  * Rewrote the Info.plist of each framework and updated the Info.plist of
    each xcframework to match the remaining architectures.
  * Merged the Objective-C members of each static library into a single
    pre-linked object file, so that they link without the -ObjC linker flag.

MediaPipeCommonGraphLibraries.xcframework:

  * Wrapped the upstream graph libraries
    (libMediaPipeTasksCommon_device_graph.a and
    libMediaPipeTasksCommon_simulator_graph.a) in a static framework with a
    generated umbrella header, module map and Info.plist, and combined them
    into an xcframework.
  * Removed the x86_64 architecture from the simulator slice.
  * Merged Objective-C members into a pre-linked object file, as above.
